  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "note": "'ola <class-5 ordinal>' ('ola lachiwiri' = 2 o'clock; ordinals match the weekday names Lachiwiri/Lachitatu/...; 1 = loyamba, 6-9 = lachisanu ndi chimodzi/chiwiri/chitatu/chinayi, 10-12 = lakhumi, lakhumi ndi chimodzi, lakhumi ndi chiwiri). Minutes additive 'ndi mphindi zisanu/khumi/makumi awiri ...', :30 = 'ndi theka'. Colloquial Malawian speech often uses English loans ('hafu pasiti 2', '2 koloko'); the written form is the native construction."
    }
  ]
